  "headline": "A 60 FPS engine frame cap closes the presentation coverage gap Q-022e named. The build holds the cap at 60.009 mean FPS with a 16.6625 ms p50 against the 16.6667 ms cap period, zero steady-driving stalls, and 3.011 ms mean render GPU time inside a 16.67 ms budget. The run nonetheless records p95_frame_ms as failed at 16.9075 ms. The declared 16.67 ms limit sits 3.3 microseconds above the cap period, so it is attainable in principle but leaves almost no room for pacing jitter; measured jitter was 241 microseconds, about 72 times that budget. Whether the limit should be restated for capped runs is an owner decision under Q-022e; this record does not change ADR-0023.",
